			"Message": "refactor(Wind/Integration): Implement structured TauriFileService and fix gRPC call implementation\n\nThis commit completes Wind's file operations abstraction by introducing TauriFileService.js, a comprehensive implementation that replaces direct Tauri filesystem APIs with Mountain backend IPC calls. The service implements the full VSCode IFileService interface using structured `mountain_ipc_invoke` commands (`file:read`, `file:write`, `file:stat`, etc.), aligning with Land's architectural principle of delegating privileged operations to the native Mountain backend.\n\nKey changes include:\n- Added TauriFileService with complete file operation methods including text/binary read/write, directory operations, file watching, and event handling\n- Fixed duplicate `performGrpcCall` method in MountainIntegrationService by removing the recursive implementation, restoring proper gRPC communication flow\n- Enhanced test suite with comprehensive file operation verification including binary data handling, directory operations, and error scenarios\n- Properly structured TypeScript test file with organized test execution and cleanup routines\n\nThese changes strengthen Wind's production readiness by establishing a robust file service layer that communicates with Mountain through structured IPC channels, enabling centralized file management while maintaining type safety and error handling.",
			"SHA": "971a92735429e4bdbc7ebd6b9e95aa349137f29e"
		},
